You know, the original discussion was whether or not it was better to
wear AoLS, ESP, or reflection.  The concept of "better" would imply that
if there is an "optimal" answer, then that would be what we're looking
for, and thus everyone's individual "admittedly non-optimal, but i like it"
strategies are probably NOT what we're looking for.

A lot of people have felt the need to introduce strawmen and/or red
herrings into the equation; for example, James trying to insist that 
not using spellcasting on all characters is not "optimal", in an effort
to prove... I dunno, some random point or other.  Sometimes I address
the off-topic assertions, because nobody is talking about the original
point.  And sometimes I recast the red herrings in light of the original
proposal, just to try to remind people of the original thread.

And often I remember that RGRN is not a very good place to hold
discussions, because of exactly that problem; people derail things onto
their own personal desired subjects.  (witness Janis' obsession)  As much
as I hate webforums, the advantage of moderation is that you can split
threads off and make it easier for those interested in the original
topic to actually follow said topic.

